{
  "name": "cloud-me",
  "description": "Diego's Cloud Me \u2014 the personal-administration half of the constellation. Where Cloud SuperApp is the launcher for everything the cloud runs, Cloud Me is the launcher for everything the PERSON runs: paperwork and money (Buro), what is due (Agenda), the public profile (Me), travel (Projects) and study (Studying), with Health in the drawer. It stores almost nothing of its own \u2014 cards live in Cloud Wallet, passwords in Cloud Vault, files in Cloud IDE, health records in Health Connect \u2014 and is the one screen that indexes all of them.",
  "category": "android",
  "build": {
    "type": "gradle",
    "entry": "build.sh"
  },
  "android": {
    "application_id": "com.diegonmarcos.cloudme",
    "compile_sdk": 36,
    "min_sdk": 26,
    "target_sdk": 35,
    "version_code": 1,
    "version_name": "0.1.0-dev",
    "abi_filters": [
      "arm64-v8a"
    ]
  },
  "signing": {
    "_doc": "ONE shared Cloud-constellation signing key for ALL Android apps (Cloud-Comms hub+forks, Cloud-Nav, Cloud-Wallet, Cloud-IDE, Cloud-SuperApp). The SAME key signs every app so cross-app signature-IPC + the in-app fleet updater never hit a signature mismatch. KEY LOCATION (raw credential + sops passwords live ONLY in the vault repo): A0_keys/providers/android/release.jks (OU=Cloud Constellation) + A0_keys/providers/android/signing.secrets.yaml. build.sh::_resolve_signing resolves $VAULT_DIR (default ~/git/cloud-vault) + sops-decrypts the passwords, exporting ANDROID_KEYSTORE_FILE/ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD/ANDROID_KEY_ALIAS/ANDROID_KEY_PASSWORD which the gradle signingConfig reads. CI does the same via a vault checkout + the SOPS_AGE_KEY secret. THERE IS NO FALLBACK: if the key is unavailable the build FAILS LOUD.",
    "vault_keystore": "A0_keys/providers/android/release.jks",
    "vault_secrets": "A0_keys/providers/android/signing.secrets.yaml"
  },
  "diagnostics": {
    "log_sink_url": "https://api.diegonmarcos.com/pub/analytics/openobserve",
    "log_sink_stream": "cloud-me",
    "enabled": true
  },
  "toolchain": {
    "_doc": "Pinned for reproducibility \u2014 all derived in flake.nix. Bump here, rebuild devShell.",
    "agp": "8.7.3",
    "gradle": "8.10.2",
    "kotlin": "2.3.20",
    "jdk": "17"
  },
  "_doc_modules": "Every libs:* entry is shared BY REFERENCE (`dir`) out of ab_cloud-libs-shared/libs \u2014 Cloud Me owns no library source of its own. That is the whole design: the app is an assembly. libs:health draws MyHealth, libs:fin draws the accounting dashboard, libs:wallet draws the Me tab's social cards, libs:cal supplies the events and todos behind Agenda. A fix in any of them lands here on the next build with no copy to keep in step.",
  "modules": {
    "app": {
      "type": "application",
      "depends_on": [
        "libs:core",
        "libs:updater",
        "libs:analytics",
        "libs:wallet",
        "libs:health",
        "libs:fin",
        "libs:cal"
      ]
    },
    "libs:core": {
      "dir": "../ab_cloud-libs-shared/libs/core",
      "type": "library"
    },
    "libs:devtools": {
      "dir": "../ab_cloud-libs-shared/libs/devtools",
      "type": "library"
    },
    "libs:updater": {
      "dir": "../ab_cloud-libs-shared/libs/updater",
      "type": "library"
    },
    "libs:analytics": {
      "dir": "../ab_cloud-libs-shared/libs/analytics",
      "type": "library"
    },
    "libs:wallet": {
      "dir": "../ab_cloud-libs-shared/libs/wallet",
      "type": "library"
    },
    "libs:health": {
      "dir": "../ab_cloud-libs-shared/libs/health",
      "type": "library"
    },
    "libs:fin": {
      "dir": "../ab_cloud-libs-shared/libs/fin",
      "type": "library"
    },
    "libs:cal": {
      "dir": "../ab_cloud-libs-shared/libs/cal",
      "type": "library"
    }
  },
  "ui": {
    "_doc": "Cloud Me's whole navigation is this block: five bottom-nav sections in `order`, everything else reached from the hamburger drawer (bottom_nav:false) or the toolbar gear (toolbar:true). A section's `pages` are its tab strip. Page CONTENT is not here \u2014 each page is a file at data/ui/<section>/<page>.json, loaded by app/build.gradle into `stack_<page id>` at build time, so a page is a page and this block stays the navigation shape alone. A section with a `target` and no `pages` (Wallet) launches another app instead of showing one. Moving Health into the bottom bar is one boolean here.",
    "permissions": {
      "runtime": [
        {
          "label": "Notifications",
          "perm": "android.permission.POST_NOTIFICATIONS"
        },
        {
          "label": "Camera",
          "perm": "android.permission.CAMERA"
        }
      ],
      "roles": []
    },
