    "default_section": "buro",
    "sections": [
      {
        "_doc": "Buro \u2014 the paperwork desk. Five tabs because the user named five concerns: the documents behind services and assets, the cards and IDs carried in a pocket, the credentials, and money split the way an accountant splits it \u2014 what HAPPENED (Accounting) against what is PLANNED (Budgeting). Buro deliberately stores nothing itself; every tab is an index into the app that already owns that data.",
        "id": "buro",
        "label": "Buro",
        "icon": "ic_nav_buro",
        "bottom_nav": true,
        "order": 1,
        "pages": [
          {
            "id": "docs",
            "label": "Docs",
            "icon": "ic_p_folder"
          },
          {
            "id": "ids",
            "label": "IDs",
            "icon": "ic_p_identities"
          },
          {
            "id": "vault",
            "label": "Vault",
            "icon": "ic_vault"
          },
          {
            "id": "accounting",
            "label": "Acct",
            "icon": "ic_fin"
          },
          {
            "id": "budgeting",
            "label": "Budget",
            "icon": "ic_p_c3_reports"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_doc": "Agenda \u2014 the only section that reads live data with no other app in front of it. Both tabs come from libs:cal: Agenda from CalEngine.events over the next 30 days, Todo from TodoStore, which is the CalDAV VTODO mirror. The user asked for the agenda and todo of Buro AND of health issues; both already land in the same CalDAV account, so the filter is a category on the item, not a second data source.",
        "id": "agenda",
        "label": "Agenda",
        "icon": "ic_nav_agenda",
        "bottom_nav": true,
        "order": 2,
        "pages": [
          {
            "id": "agenda",
            "label": "Agenda",
            "icon": "ic_p_cal_day"
          },
          {
            "id": "todo",
            "label": "Todo",
            "icon": "ic_p_more"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_doc": "Me \u2014 the app's namesake and its centre slot. One page: the social cards from libs:wallet's Me tab, the same deck Cloud Wallet shows, sourced from ui.socials and mirroring front-diegonmarcos/b-Media/mySocials. It is the public half of the wallet, which is why it is shared code rather than a second implementation.",
        "id": "me",
        "label": "Me",
        "icon": "ic_nav_me",
        "bottom_nav": true,
        "order": 3,
        "pages": [
          {
            "id": "me",
            "label": "Me",
            "icon": "ic_nav_me"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_doc": "Projects \u2014 what is being worked on, travelled to, or studied. Studying leads because it is the standing project; Trips is the one with a date, and History is its record. Studying was a bottom-nav section of its own until it became a tab here \u2014 study management is a project, and the freed bar slot went to Wallet, which is a different app entirely.",
        "id": "projects",
        "label": "Projects",
        "icon": "ic_nav_trips",
        "bottom_nav": true,
        "order": 4,
        "pages": [
          {
            "id": "studying",
            "label": "Studying",
            "icon": "ic_nav_studying"
          },
          {
            "id": "trips",
            "label": "Trips",
            "icon": "ic_nav_trips"
          },
          {
            "id": "history",
            "label": "History",
            "icon": "ic_map_pin"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_doc": "Wallet \u2014 the only bar item that is not a destination. It has no `pages`; its `target` is handed to MainActivity.onTarget, which launches Cloud Wallet. The deck, its expiry dates and its QR codes live in that app, and the bar slot Studying vacated is worth more as one tap to it than as a second copy of it here.",
